column63:
I've never liked the aesthetics of a leading comma....<p><pre><code>  var foo = {
        bar: 100
      , baz: 200
  };
</code></pre>
However the fact that (some) Javascript engines don't like trailing commas...<p><pre><code>  var foo = {
      bar: 100,
      baz: 200,    // this borked the last time I tried it!
  };
</code></pre>
causes me no end of trouble coming from regular Perl usage where they are allowed (and recommended best practise).
